# Line endings. Every text file is checked out with \n line endings on every platform, as it is stored. Without this, a Windows checkout
# (core.autocrlf=true on the hosted runners) wrote \r\n into test sources and fixtures, so a raw string literal in a test held \r\n on the
# Windows CI legs and \n on Linux, and a test that matched a line by its "\n" passed on one and failed on the other (runs 652 to 680).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files kept byte for byte as they were exported, \r\n included: two scanner exports the importer's \r\n handling is tested on, and the
# archive of superseded material.
tests/Tempest.Calc.Tests.Import/Samples/scan/gom-two-stage.csv -text
tests/Tempest.Calc.Tests.Import/Samples/scan/zeiss-groove.csv -text
archive/** -text
